[0.000, "o", "\u001b[39;49m\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[H\u001b[2J\u001b[27d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[37m\u001b[44mCards: \u001b[30m\u001b[47mA\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[30m\u001b[47m3\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[30m\u001b[47m8\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[30m\u001b[47m10\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[30m\u001b[47mQ\u001b[37m\u001b[44m\u001b[45X\u001b[27;63H38 cards in deck  \u001b[28;9H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1K "]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[31m\u001b[47m3\u001b[37m\u001b[44m   \u001b[31m\u001b[47m10\u001b[37m\u001b[44m\u001b[49X\u001b[28;65H"]
[0.000, "o", "I have 5 cards  \u001b[29d\b"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1K\u001b[30d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1K\u001b[28d\b\u001b[39;49m\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\u001b[10dThis is the traditional children's card game \"Go Fish\". We each get\r\u001b[11d"]
[0.000, "o", "seven cards, and the rest of the deck is kept to be drawn from later. The\r\u001b[12dobject of the game is to collect \"books\", or all of the cards of a single\r\u001b[13d"]
[0.000, "o", "value. For example, getting four 2's would give you a \"book of 2's\".\r\u001b[15d"]
[0.000, "o", "We take turns asking each other for cards, but you can only ask me for\r\u001b[16d"]
[0.000, "o", "a card value you already have. If I have any, I must give them to you,\r\u001b[17dand you can keep asking. If you ask me for a card value I don't have,\r\u001b[18d"]
[0.000, "o", "then I'll tell you to \"Go Fish!\", which means that you draw a card from\r\u001b[19d"]
[0.000, "o", "the deck. If you draw the card you asked me for, you get to keep asking\r\u001b[20d"]
[0.000, "o", "me for cards. If not, then it's my turn. The game stops when one of us\r\u001b[21d"]
[0.000, "o", "runs out of cards, and the winner is the one with the most books.\r\u001b[23d"]
[0.000, "o", "You ask for a card by typing its name (a234567891jqk), type x to quit,\r\u001b[25dYou get to start.\r\u001b[26d"]
